{"task_id": "HumanEval/16", "solution": "def count_distinct_characters(string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\" Given a string, find out how many distinct characters (regardless of case) does it consist of\n    >>> count_distinct_characters('xyzXYZ')\n    3\n    >>> count_distinct_characters('Jerry')\n    4\n    \"\"\"\n    import unicodedata\n\n    # Normalize the string to a canonical form (NFC) and convert to casefolded for case-insensitivity.\n    normalized_string = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFC\", string).casefold()\n    # Create a set of characters to count distinct ones, then return its size.\n    return len(set(normalized_string))"}
