{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "def iscube(a):\n    '''\n    Checks if an integer 'a' is a perfect cube.\n    Uses an integer cube root calculation with correctional adjustments to handle large numbers and floating-point precision.\n    '''\n    if a < 0:\n        negative = True\n        n = -a\n    else:\n        negative = False\n        n = a\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Calculate an initial candidate for the cube root using floating-point.\n    # This is a good starting point, but needs integer correction.\n    c = int(round(n ** (1/3)))\n\n    # Adjust the candidate to find the correct integer cube root.\n    # Ensure c^3 <= n < (c+1)^3 for positive n.\n    while (c + 1) ** 3 <= n:\n        c += 1\n    while c ** 3 > n:\n        c -= 1\n\n    # Check if the cube of the integer root matches the original number.\n    # Account for the original sign.\n    if negative:\n        return (-c) ** 3 == a\n    else:\n        return c ** 3 == a"}
